    hgTitle: "Districtwide Supper Program Expansion to All Campuses",
    hgText:
      "Killeen ISD's proposed FY 2027 budget states that the Supper Program (CACFP) will be expanded 'to all campuses with 40% student participation goal.' In the School Nutrition Fund section, the materials further note that the Community Child and Adult Care Food Program (Supper Program) 'will be offered at 45 locations' and references approximately 472 cafeteria staff and 33 central office staff. This indicates a substantial expansion of school nutrition operations that may require outside vendor support for food service supplies, food products, distribution, equipment, or related operational services.\n\nThe districtwide nature of the expansion suggests possible procurement needs tied to meal production, delivery logistics, kitchen or serving equipment, packaging, point-of-service support, or other nutrition program infrastructure necessary to support broader CACFP supper availability. Even where staffing is internal, a program expansion to all campuses commonly creates vendor opportunities in food purchasing and ancillary services.\n\nNo separate contract value is listed, and no procurement date is stated. However, the expansion is presented as part of the FY 2026-27 proposed budget and includes a clear implementation objective—expanding the supper program to all campuses and targeting 40% student participation.",
