    hgTitle: "Public Auditorium Food and Beverage Concession",
    hgText:
      'Ordinance 912-2026 authorizes the Director of Parks and Recreation to enter into "one or more concession agreements for the operation of a first-class food and beverage service in the Public Auditorium," for a period not to exceed three years, with two one-year options to renew.\n\nThis is a clear upcoming service opportunity for concessionaires, hospitality operators, food service vendors, and event-support providers. The ordinance specifically contemplates one or more agreements and defines the service area as first-class food and beverage operations in a City venue.\n\nPotential work may include concession management, staffing, catering-style service, point-of-sale operations, equipment provisioning, menu planning, inventory management, and event-day operations. The term structure of up to three years with two one-year renewal options makes this a meaningful procurement opportunity with a defined service period.',
