    hgTitle: "Culinary Incubator and Food Hub Development",
    hgText:
      "During the public hearing for rezoning case Z(CD)-01-25, City staff presented a City-submitted conditional rezoning for approximately 0.820 acres at 228 McGill Ave., 234 McGill Ave., 438 Allison St., and 445 Allison St. for development of a culinary incubator and food hub with associated parking. Staff stated that the structures on the properties have already been demolished and the land cleared for the project. The proposed facility would be 8,624 square feet and include space for a culinary incubator, retail section, and container village.\n\nThe project was described as a public-nonprofit partnership intended to create an educational facility for prospective entrepreneurs to gain skills and knowledge for successful culinary businesses. The City Manager stated that the City is still working with various funding agencies to procure funds from nonprofits and federal sources, with some remaining funding gap that may require eventual City contribution, and that staff are not yet ready to present the full financial picture.\n\nAlthough final funding is not complete, this is a strong early-stage pipeline opportunity for architecture, engineering, construction, site development, parking, utilities, fit-out, food-service related infrastructure, modular/container improvements, and possibly owner’s rep or grant-related consulting support.",
