    hgTitle: "Jail North Reopening Could Drive Facility and Operational Procurements",
    hgText:
      'Under the Manager\'s Report, the agenda lists "Reopening of Jail North to House Growing Inmate Population," with an attached presentation titled "SHF-BOCC Presentation North Activation 8.26.2026." This indicates the county is planning or discussing the activation of Jail North in response to rising inmate population needs.\n\nReopening a detention facility commonly creates service and product purchasing needs beyond direct county staffing, including detention facility activation support, equipment, furnishings, security-related systems, medical and operational supplies, food service support, janitorial or sanitation services, maintenance, repairs, inspections, and other startup or operational contracting needs. The agenda wording makes clear this is a forward-looking operational initiative rather than a purely historical report.\n\nWhile the agenda does not itself identify a specific solicitation, budget amount, or vendor, the reopening of a jail to increase housing capacity is a substantial government action that could reasonably lead to one or more future procurements tied to facility readiness and ongoing contracted services.',
